**Finding this round**
Option (c) (checking the impedance exactly before placing) adds nothing new at a depth of one step. Rungs 1–3 already get the exact one-step effect of every add and remove as inputs and add it to the action scores (`decap_loop/modal_env.py`, `decap_loop/model.py`). A new version would have to draft several placements ahead and then recompute the resonance peaks. That is close to the improvement loops in DACT/NeuRewriter, which the design document already treats as not a contribution. I added this to PROPOSALS.md.

**Decision** (logged in PROGRESS.md): I am not building (c) until r3a and r2a have been judged. The rule is one change at a time, the GPU queue already holds about 20 hours of training, and there is no free CPU slot for a test run.

